647 - Mine Eyes Have Seen the Glory
 / 
Key: Bb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 647
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
Mine eyes have seen the glory of the coming of the Lord;
He is [Eb]trampling out the vintage where the [Bb]grapes of wrath are stored;
He hath loosed the fateful lightning of his terrible swift sword;
His [Eb]truth is [F]marching [Bb]on.
[Bb]Glory, glory, hallelujah! [Eb]Glory, glory, halle[Bb]lujah!
[Bb]Glory, glory, hallelujah! His [Eb]truth is [F]marching [Bb]on.

Refrain:
Glory! Glory! Hallelujah! Glory! Glory! Hallelujah!
[Eb]Glory! Glory! Hallelujah! His [Bb]truth is marching on.

Verse 2:
He has sounded forth the trumpet that shall never call retreat;
[Eb]He is sifting out the hearts [Bb]of men before His judgment seat;
O be swift, my soul, to answer Him! be jubilant, my feet!
[Eb]Our [F]God is [Bb]marching on.

Verse 3:
In the beauty of the lilies Christ was born across the sea,
[Eb]With a glory in His [Bb]bosom that transfigures you and me;
As He died to make men holy, let us live to make men free!
[Eb]While [F]God is [Bb]marching on.
